<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuri II Boleslav</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1308–<a href="/years/1340">1340</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Bolesław-Jerzy II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuri II Boleslav was the last ruler of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volhynia">Volhynia</a>, from 1323 until his death in 1340. Born Bolesław, a Masovian Piast prince whose mother was a daughter of Yuri I, he converted to Orthodoxy on taking the throne. His reliance on foreign advisers angered the boyars, who poisoned him, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> then divided his realm.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yuri-ii-boleslav.jpg" alt="Yuri II Boleslav" width="320" height="357" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: K. R. v. Siegl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yurii_II_Boleslav_seal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
